    {
      "request_id": "v181:matplotlib__matplotlib-24149:DEEPSEEK_NT_S1_M3_R_V181_B5000K:20261109180002:member_001:0034",
      "tool": "fix_patch",
      "arguments": {
        "task_ids": [],
        "message": "Fix gh-24163: ax.bar raises for all-nan data (cbook._safe_first_finite leaked StopIteration).\n\nRoot cause: `cbook._safe_first_finite` used `return next(val for val in obj if safe_isfinite(val))`. When no element is finite, `next()` raises StopIteration, which escapes into callers and (per the issue traceback) surfaces to users as `StopIteration` from `Axes.bar` via `_convert_dx`.\n\nCore fix — lib/matplotlib/cbook/__init__.py:\n  Replace the `next(...)` generator expression with an explicit loop that raises\n  `ValueError(\"No finite values found\")` when the input contains no finite value.\n  StopIteration therefore can no longer leak out of this helper.\n\nCallers that intentionally relied on the old \"no usable first element -> just\ncarry on\" behavior now also catch ValueError (behavior otherwise unchanged):\n\n  - lib/matplotlib/axes/_axes.py `Axes._convert_dx`: added ValueError to both\n    except clauses (x0 and xconv). This is the path from the issue traceback.\n  - lib/matplotlib/units.py `Registry.get_converter`: added ValueError so an\n    empty input (e.g. `ax.bar([], [])`) still returns None as before.\n  - lib/matplotlib/dates.py `DateConverter.default_units`: added ValueError so\n    empty datetime data still yields default units (e.g. `plt.scatter` with an\n    empty datetime64 array).\n\nRegression tests added:\n  - test_cbook.py::test_safe_first_finite_no_finite_value (parametrized over\n    [], [nan], [None], [inf, nan]) asserts ValueError(\"No finite values found\")\n    rather than a leaked StopIteration.\n  - test_axes.py::test_bar_all_nan reproduces the issue exactly:\n    ax.bar([np.nan], [np.nan]) yields one Rectangle with nan x and height, and\n    ax.bar([np.nan], [0]) also succeeds.\n\nVerification on this exact version (v7): 7/7 selected target tests pass\n(test_bar_all_nan, test_safe_first_finite_no_finite_value x4,\ntest_bar_ticklabel_fail, test_units empty_arrays). A broader 167-test run over\ntest_cbook/test_axes/test_units/test_dates passed all issue-relevant tests,\nincluding bar_timedelta, bar_ticklabel_fail, all datetime/units/dates cases and\ntest_cbook test_safe_first_element*; its only 2 failures are\nTest_callback_registry::test_registration_on_non_empty_registry[True/False],\nwhich fail with `AttributeError: 'Test_callback_registry' object has no\nattribute 'callbacks'` -- an unrelated pre-existing test-fixture defect in\ncallback/weakref machinery, untouched by this change."
      },
